Shared services run once per repository, in a Compose project of their own, and
are connected to each worktree whose services use them: declare them under
[shared] in treerig.toml. `treerig up` starts the ones a worktree uses; these
commands start, replace, stop and inspect them yourself.

Usage:
  treerig shared [flags]
  treerig shared [command]

Available Commands:
  up          start shared services, and reconnect every worktree that uses them
              (--recreate <name> replaces a running one)
  down        stop shared services; their data is kept unless you pass --volumes
  status      show the shared services: state, addresses, definition and
              connection

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for shared

Global Flags:
      --progress mode   how to show progress: auto (redraw on a terminal) or
                        plain (one line per change) (default "auto")
  -v, --verbose         show what treerig runs, and every detail

Use "treerig shared [command] --help" for more information about a command.
